 "poem": "Or a lingering heave of breathing,\nOr the shafts that flit in darkness\nFrom the edges of shadowed hills.\nThe wild wind whispers, buzzing\nIn the distance and rolling over\nThe distant hill-top's edge,\nAnd a shuddering breath disappears.\nI hear a voice.  Away from again!\nA sound like a sudden sudden\nGibbering with laughter at again,\nWith an exultant melody.\nAh, but is it never",
